  "doc.title": "Why SATA Has Lasted Over Twenty Years · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "Why is a seven-pin data cable, with a host interface fixed in 2004, still what the largest hard drives plug into in 2026? Seven models you can drag: the timing budget of a parallel bus, an 8b/10b encoder, the frames of one read command, NCQ on a spinning platter, link power states, a port multiplier, and how far a hard disk is from 6 Gb/s.",
